A||||5||86SE||4cyl wont start - it gets gas and spark - HELP!!||||1||
Z||000000||86SE||06-01-2000||02:08 AM||||I have been workin a 84 4cyl Fiero. It has 119995.7 miles, it gets fuel and im sure it has a spark.<BR>I can see the main injector on the carb shoot gas into the carb. And I took out the all the spark plugs and turned it over and all 4 of em sparked. But 2 plugs were wet.<P>I have tried adjusting the timeing and I got it to just barely fire. It feels like it will fire, just not quite.<P>There is also a smell of fuel from the exhaust tips after i crank on it. And after it feels like it will start, white smoke comes from around/near the distributor (smells like burnt fuel).<P>Any help will be greatly appreciated!!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-01-2000||09:55 AM||||still sound like an ignition problem. plugs take more to fire in a compressed cylinder than in open air.<P>smoke from around the distributor is odd. Can't think of anything that would cause that. check the wiring and stuff carfully. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||lennyb4||06-01-2000||10:24 AM||||Sounds like a bad coil to me. Check the color of the spark. Blue its good, orange its weak. I had the same problem last spring. I checked and sure enough my coil had a little crack in it, just enough to let moisture in. The reason you smell fuel out the exaust is because your missing and not burning all the gas. ****WATCH out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> when you finally do get it started, if you have build up in your exaust you could blow your converter/muffler apart (trust me im speaking from experiance)As for the smoke around the dist???? got me??||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||06-01-2000||01:23 PM||||The spark is orange.  I already too a coil from my other car and brought it over there to see if it would fire but it dident.  I'll clean and re-gap the plugs and put the new coil on it to see if it will fire.<P>Andways, when i took the plugs out to see if they would spark, only one had a solid spark, but it was still orange/blue.  The other 3 sparks jumped around, not lookin like they had good contact.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||06-01-2000||01:29 PM||||Also you might want to take a close look at the wires.||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||06-01-2000||03:18 PM||||Hey wait a minute, I forgot to mention the ECMs codes.  It gets a code 33 or 34 for the MAP sensor.  The MAP sensor controls the ignition timing and fuel delivery doesnt it?<P>I'll switch the bad one from the 4cyl with mine from my v-6 and see if it starts.||||reg||3
